#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128959 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "7dcea6be-fd16-5312-b50c-157bafcc2d65" :question/math-academy-id "e-8189" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$, given by\n$R = \\Big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}∫_{0}^{yz}dxdzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x = 0}^{x = yz}dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yzdzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}y[\\frac{z^{2}}{2}]_{z = 0}^{z = \\sqrt{2y}}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}(\\sqrt{2y})^{2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}y^{2}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{y = 1}^{y = 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(8 - 1) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128960 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "b0ad2f24-6f0c-5d66-9312-5e41840b4fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8190" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/833b93599de9c6b708f3a1261e746f92.png)\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/2298616a278bfc40c45434c5731feaf7.png)\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/cc9d4db3f6570233d1e1e71d8636bcdc.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{4 - x - y}dzdydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[z]_{z = 0}^{z = 4 - x - y}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}(4 - x - y) - 0dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - x - ydydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[(4 - x)y - \\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 2}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}((4 - x)(2) - \\frac{2^{2}}{2}) - 0dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}6 - 2xdx \\\\\n&= [6x - x^{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= (6(1) - 1^{2}) - 0 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128961 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "7883263b-110b-558f-83b2-0f6ec28be2c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8191" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface $y=xz$, the plane $y=2$, and the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $z=0$, $z=1$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: xz \\leq y \\leq 2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{xz}^{2}dydzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}[y]_{y = xz}^{y = 2}dzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}2 - xzdzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[2z - \\frac{xz^{2}}{2}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[2(1 - 0) - (x(1^{2} - 0))/(2)]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2 - \\frac{x}{2}dx \\\\\n&= [2x - \\frac{x^{2}}{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= (2 - \\frac{1}{4}) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd971463-dabf-59c6-92da-afc33c6414e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128001} {:answer/id #uuid "0e9c1c01-63e7-554d-b7b5-ea5d06e6cf1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128002} {:answer/id #uuid "2d777545-8119-5ee9-b4fe-f81465899dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128003} {:answer/id #uuid "51159f23-7b3e-5baa-89d2-f3d1a2d19b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128004} {:answer/id #uuid "55d6d7e6-5337-5cd3-960a-5900b068af67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51159f23-7b3e-5baa-89d2-f3d1a2d19b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128004} :answer-field/id #uuid "131495b6-5f7f-5b8e-911d-2fe07629cc84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128000}] :question/id #uuid "cfdc548b-2292-576d-ab60-511ad802a9dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-40327" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$, given by\n\n$R = {(x, y, z): - 2 \\le y \\le 0, 0 \\le z \\le 2 + y, 1 \\le x \\le y - z + 3}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e55498f-ee29-5d2d-a06a-1958a3c9382a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128007} {:answer/id #uuid "f2fcbc4a-b71e-57f0-a0fd-86c705ec9d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128008} {:answer/id #uuid "00076a9e-0ce5-5fed-9dfe-9ddb3a5dbc60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128009} {:answer/id #uuid "05b75bb3-df6e-5656-90ac-f9071a71be59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128010} {:answer/id #uuid "59c86409-a8a6-52a2-a6a7-ae6463b43ae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b75bb3-df6e-5656-90ac-f9071a71be59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128010} :answer-field/id #uuid "13dc572f-4517-579c-807e-86aa3140aa69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128006}] :question/id #uuid "a3a27fdc-218a-5216-8272-6169534abedb" :question/math-academy-id "q-40353" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/q-40353.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*"}]}
